=== curate-dev
DISABLE_PROMPT_CACHING=1
cwd=<WORK>/root
arg: -p
arg: --model
arg: haiku
arg: --system-prompt
arg: You curate the memory of one AgentSI agent. Memory is a list of items with ids; you never rewrite it.
Return deltas only: `add` new items, `retire` items by id with a reason, mark ids `helpful` or `harmful`.
Propose only deltas backed by the listed signals. Every add cites in `evidence` at least one signal ref exactly as listed.
Learn from failures as well as successes: an accepted mark shows what to keep doing, a failure or a rejection shows what to avoid.
Retire items that are stale, duplicated or contradicted by the signals. Status snapshots (pending work, dates of today) do not belong in memory.
At most 5 adds and 10 retires. Write new item texts in the language of the existing items, one short sentence each.
Empty arrays are a valid answer.
arg: --no-session-persistence
arg: --safe-mode
arg: --restricted
arg: --strict-mcp-config
arg: --disable-slash-commands
arg: --permission-mode
arg: dontAsk
arg: --permission-prompts
arg: none
arg: --max-budget-usd
arg: 0.1
arg: --tools=
arg: --effort
arg: low
arg: --json-schema
arg: {"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["add","retire","helpful","harmful"],"properties":{"add":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["text","kind","evidence"],"properties":{"text":{"type":"string"},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["fact","lesson"]},"evidence":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}}}},"retire":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["id","why"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"why":{"type":"string"}}}},"helpful":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"harmful":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}}}
